  "rationale": "The spec needs 32 Msps sustained throughput (32 requests every 1 us tick) and all 32 results back within 0.5 us of the tick. Only pipelined and pipelined_m produce 1 result/cycle, so they are the only families that can meet the throughput constraint without requiring Fmax > 32 MHz (pipelined) or > 32 MHz (pipelined_m). The accuracy constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-12 = 0.000244141 requires roughly 12+ effective bits; CORDIC with N=12..16 micro-rotations and W=14..18 with modest guards should cover this. Area is the primary objective, so I focus on the low-W, low-N end of the feasible accuracy region. pipelined_m with m=2..4 trades a small latency increase for significant FF/area savings, making it a strong area-minimiser candidate. I split the budget evenly between the two families to map the trade-off between full pipeline latency (lower latency, more FFs) and partial pipeline (higher latency, fewer FFs) and find where the area front bends. The sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 us constraint is the tightest system constraint: at Fmax = 64 MHz, 10 cycles = 156 ns, leaving ample margin for 32 results in 0.5 us; at Fmax = 32 MHz, 10 cycles = 312 ns, still within 0.5 us. So both families should have feasible points, and the search will reveal the exact area/accuracy/latency trade-off."
}

