  "rationale": "The exploration has successfully identified a feasible Pareto front that satisfies all system and accuracy constraints. The best design (pipelined, data_width=18, n_iter=15) achieves an area of 44,494 um^2, which is well below the hypervolume reference of 100,000 um^2, and provides 13.3 bits of accuracy, exceeding the 12-bit reference and the 2^-12 error constraint. The system constraint (sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 us) is met by the top designs (best seen 0.301 us), and throughput is sufficient (138 MSPS > 32 MSPS). Since this is the final round and the front covers the trade-off space effectively with a clear minimum-area candidate for the selection rule, stopping is the appropriate action."
